course: dictionary
lesson: 1114
title: Brazil: a country and a nut
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one you need. Look for a capital letter and a clue. «The eastern bulge of Brazil lay east of the Tordesillas line.» Here Brazil starts with a capital letter and names a place, so it means the country.
explain: Now read «Brazil nuts» in a shop, or «a brazil» in a sentence about a tree. Brazil with a small b and a plural like brazils is a nut, not a country. The sentence tells you: a brazil is a large, hard, three-sided nut from a tall South American tree.
explain: Brazil is a proper noun, the name of one particular place, so it always starts with a capital letter. Ask yourself: is this a name or a thing? When you can see which, you can work out the meaning. Then check by swapping your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Brazil is the biggest country in South America.
fact: People in Brazil mostly speak Portuguese, while most of South America speaks Spanish.
fact: The capital of Brazil is Brasília.
fact: A brazil, or Brazil nut, is a large, hard, three-sided nut from a tall South American tree.
fact: A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «The eastern bulge of Brazil lay east of the Tordesillas line, which is a main reason Brazil speaks Portuguese.» What language do most people in Brazil speak? | French | Spanish | English | *Portuguese
exercise: What is the capital city of Brazil? | Salvador | Rio de Janeiro | *Brasília | São Paulo
exercise: «The Pantanal in Brazil is the world's biggest tropical wetland.» What is the Pantanal? | A desert | *A huge tropical wetland | A city by the sea | A tall mountain
test: In «Wild capuchin monkeys in Brazil crack hard nuts with stones», what is Brazil? | A nut from a tree | A monkey | A stone tool | *A country
test: On a world map, what does the bulge of Brazil tuck into? | *The curve of West Africa | The coast of Europe | The Amazon River | The Pacific Ocean
exam: Which sentence is true? | Brazil is a small city in Africa | Brazil is a fruit that grows on a bush | *Brazil is the biggest country in South America | Brazil nuts come from a short tree in Europe
